                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb0736aa-7730-4691-aa91-78d999566aa6",
                        "source_entry_id": "abc0a41d-03b1-3c25-ad7c-e646e1d54c5c",
                        "source_sense_id": "9342a702-c235-3004-a455-5a578967da11",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ausgrabung",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ausgrabung",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7fceed3-6aa6-3138-b1c5-f12a602f104a",
                                        "entry_id": "fd5ebb36-4b91-3933-87fa-3a25961fd4b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Stelle, an der Ruinen oder Fossilien freigelegt wurden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "656b16a1-42b2-472b-a41f-979d0a7847f3",
                                                "sense_id": "b7fceed3-6aa6-3138-b1c5-f12a602f104a",
                                                "text": "Morgen geht es zur Besichtigung der Ausgrabungen im Norden der Insel."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e8a2f1f-9241-3e15-b326-9ea30ff69007",
                                        "entry_id": "fd5ebb36-4b91-3933-87fa-3a25961fd4b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "das Freilegen von Vorgeschichtlichem (zum Beispiel Ruinen oder Siedlungen) oder Fossilien"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d593070-dfcb-48cb-810e-55f1d733c795",
                                                "sense_id": "1e8a2f1f-9241-3e15-b326-9ea30ff69007",
                                                "text": "„Wo schriftliche Überlieferungen fehlen, helfen uns die Archäologen mit ihren Ausgrabungen weiter.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7c5ef0c-06b8-404d-83fa-63f93a41a62c",
                                                "sense_id": "1e8a2f1f-9241-3e15-b326-9ea30ff69007",
                                                "text": "Im Sommer wird Marlies an einer Ausgrabung in Polen teilnehmen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca69a966-ffa9-4935-88ba-66a5be2eecb3",
                                                "sense_id": "1e8a2f1f-9241-3e15-b326-9ea30ff69007",
                                                "text": "Es ist noch unklar, wie das Institut die geplanten Ausgrabungen in Trier finanzieren will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e31a290c-fc56-4715-bf79-15d42f307105",
                                                "sense_id": "1e8a2f1f-9241-3e15-b326-9ea30ff69007",
                                                "text": "„Meyer leitet die Ausgrabungen am Harzhorn, wo im Jahr 233 Germanen und Römer erbittert gegeneinander wüteten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a131a446-88c8-4e51-a42e-c75d1b29aa74",
                                                "sense_id": "1e8a2f1f-9241-3e15-b326-9ea30ff69007",
                                                "text": "„Archäologen entdeckten den Ort 1966 auf Luftbildaufnahmen, Ausgrabungen erbrachten Gräben mit 150 und 180 m Länge, die einen rechteckigen Bezirk abgrenzen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a7f00a0-a64d-44df-8b7f-4172c7fdf51e",
                                                "sense_id": "1e8a2f1f-9241-3e15-b326-9ea30ff69007",
                                                "text": "„Bei Ausgrabungen in Manching stießen Archäologen auf das winzige Knöchelchen eines Fisches.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41fa3fd3-c6c5-3a15-aed6-32a42f80aeaa",
                                        "entry_id": "fd5ebb36-4b91-3933-87fa-3a25961fd4b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "übertragen, das Hervorholen von etwas längst Vergessenem"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09266f4e-8cf6-4f0b-a18b-2fd15eab8597",
                                                "sense_id": "41fa3fd3-c6c5-3a15-aed6-32a42f80aeaa",
                                                "text": "Die Ausgrabung dieses alten Schmökers hättest du dir sparen können."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4b63090-23de-47ad-9107-c8f3b7299e37",
                        "source_entry_id": "abc0a41d-03b1-3c25-ad7c-e646e1d54c5c",
                        "source_sense_id": "9342a702-c235-3004-a455-5a578967da11",
                        "target_lang_word": "excavation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "excavation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fa2bd54-59e2-3695-beaa-268e50f6e337",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of excavating, or of making hollow, by cutting, scooping, or digging out a part of a solid mass."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2233097-f804-4464-a640-17119458c0fe",
                                                "sense_id": "2fa2bd54-59e2-3695-beaa-268e50f6e337",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: hollowing out, hollowing"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b86009a6-3acb-37eb-bcb7-b926d2a809a3",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of excavating, or of making hollow, by cutting, scooping, or digging out a part of a solid mass.",
                                            "Especially, the trade of digging engineered holes for building foundations, roadbed preparations, and similar purposes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33d01032-c6f4-3e10-bd2b-ec530e3ebc47",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cavity formed by cutting, digging, or scooping."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3a73443-5691-4c7f-a069-61fe7b7b9412",
                                                "sense_id": "33d01032-c6f4-3e10-bd2b-ec530e3ebc47",
                                                "text": "Prof. Dainelli made a personal study of the lakes of the Upper Indus lying between its confluence with the Gilgit on the west and the plains of Kashmir on the east. From this district he cites fifty lakes and groups of lakes. Many of these are moraine-dammed, but some of the larger ones, as the Satpor Tso, the Tso Moriri, the Chiun Tso, and the group of lakes associated with the Pángong Tso, he considers to have originated by glacial excavation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65f37c39-b4d2-31a8-a02e-9cadde7276fc",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An uncovered cutting in the earth, in distinction from a covered cutting or tunnel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cdef6a2f-fb92-331a-9981-24c8e3c61314",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The material dug out in making a channel or cavity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48a13427-54e2-4be4-9a47-640a5d61d4a5",
                                                "sense_id": "cdef6a2f-fb92-331a-9981-24c8e3c61314",
                                                "text": "[…] to cart away the excavations from the work, and to recart the same back again so far as required to fill the trench over the sewer […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a74a6569-4a18-368f-831f-a692a206ce79",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Archaeological research that unearths buildings, tombs and objects of historical value."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1f818d5-c760-3c6b-bfa3-6acf2b8309f8",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A site where an archaeological exploration is being carried out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03b0c45a-8156-4d61-ab0b-1dee5b0954bf",
                                                "sense_id": "b1f818d5-c760-3c6b-bfa3-6acf2b8309f8",
                                                "text": "Gregory led the excavations alongside marine archaeologist Andreas Kallmeyer Bloch, who is also a curator at the National Museum.\n“It’s been a long process and I’ve come close to giving up along the way, but this is undoubtedly the craziest archaeological excavation I’ve yet been part of,” Bloch said in the news release."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c02bb0df-d0ab-3864-80b6-e1f59f9a7012",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something uncovered by archaeological excavation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd39d8fb-7d95-4c85-a354-82aa5e55043e",
                                                "sense_id": "c02bb0df-d0ab-3864-80b6-e1f59f9a7012",
                                                "text": "To date, [Taco's 1982 cover of Irving Berlin's 1935] \"Cheek To Cheek\" and similar auditory excavations have fared poorly."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d656ca0f-e4d3-3df3-9737-91c3e9404134",
                                        "entry_id": "3e633d00-42fb-30ce-9ed7-9a379f1dc419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of discovering and exposing or developing (a quality)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84de7031-e145-474c-b5f9-765a050658fc",
                                                "sense_id": "d656ca0f-e4d3-3df3-9737-91c3e9404134",
                                                "text": "Chua looks at the landscape of childhood rather like a mining engineer looks at a pristine landscape—ripe for the excavation of talent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26a4d4b9-6caf-48f8-b2df-5c3b8e008d7b",
                                                "sense_id": "d656ca0f-e4d3-3df3-9737-91c3e9404134",
                                                "text": "This Andrade, a lawyer, seemed to enjoy bureucratic process as much as Mário de Andrade valorized the enthnographic excavation of creativity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "614b912d-af63-4df7-b236-13253ee82ca0",
                                                "sense_id": "d656ca0f-e4d3-3df3-9737-91c3e9404134",
                                                "text": "In the same vein, Emirbayer and Desmond (2012) highlight the vital need for deeper scholarly reflexivity as regards race, advocating excavation of hidden presuppositions at social, disciplinary and scholastic levels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f08cc7b-1f78-4c18-b39d-f56dde1bceae",
                        "source_entry_id": "abc0a41d-03b1-3c25-ad7c-e646e1d54c5c",
                        "source_sense_id": "9342a702-c235-3004-a455-5a578967da11",
                        "target_lang_word": "exhumation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exhumation",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a27c90ea-a4cd-3e9b-99e9-f731650bfc3c",
                                        "entry_id": "29e38c34-a0da-3a27-9fe2-d1e5d0c00f1d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action d’exhumer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Administration"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e0be1a8-6e07-4544-85d1-b0261f8fe79e",
                                                "sense_id": "a27c90ea-a4cd-3e9b-99e9-f731650bfc3c",
                                                "text": "D'où venait cet ossuaire? M. Ledru avait présidé à l'exhumation des rois à Saint-Denis, et il avait pris dans chaque tombeau ce qui lui avait plu."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b99009a2-c6fb-463b-b815-26cff87aabb6",
                                                "sense_id": "a27c90ea-a4cd-3e9b-99e9-f731650bfc3c",
                                                "text": "Selon les termes de la loi sur les sépultures militaires, seul le secrétariat d'État aux Anciens Combattants et Victimes de guerre est habilité à procéder à l’exhumation des sépultures militaires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2249bb63-da72-49ae-a24f-b3e2159c55d2",
                                                "sense_id": "a27c90ea-a4cd-3e9b-99e9-f731650bfc3c",
                                                "text": "Geneviève était malgache, et lui avait parlé des curieuses coutumes d’exhumation pratiquées dans son pays. Une semaine après le décès on déterrait le cadavre, on défaisait les linges qui l’entouraient et on prenait un repas en sa présence, dans la salle à manger familiale ; puis on l’enterrait de nouveau. On recommençait au bout d’un mois, puis de trois, il ne se souvenait plus très bien mais il lui semblait qu’il n’y avait pas moins de sept exhumations successives, la dernière se déroulant un an après le décès, avant que le défunt ne soit définitivement considéré comme mort, et ne puisse accéder à l’éternel repos."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7fcb28e-1e7b-34ce-a2fc-041ed4e0d651",
                                        "entry_id": "29e38c34-a0da-3a27-9fe2-d1e5d0c00f1d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action de retrouver ou de ressortir des choses anciennes ou longtemps inutilisées."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf11c10b-0661-467a-90ad-052e138fcfea",
                                                "sense_id": "b7fcb28e-1e7b-34ce-a2fc-041ed4e0d651",
                                                "text": "Mais Amélie […] était tout à l’excitation de ce reportage, à l’exhumation du passé, à la rencontre de ces francs-maçons mystérieux, dont elle ne savait guère que ce qu'en racontaient les journaux dans leurs « marronniers » annuels sur les « frères trois points ». Y avait-il des « sœurs » maçonnes pendant la guerre ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
